The attached image (Fig. 5) demonstrates Nano-11's ability to facilitate antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Flow cytometry plots (A) show increased percentages and mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA-containing cells in lymph nodes when OVA is adjuvanted with Nano-11, outperforming OVA alone and aluminum hydroxide (AH) on both day 1 and day 2. Bar charts confirm that Nano-11 significantly boosts the MFI of OVA within antigen-presenting cells (B) and increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells (C), indicating enhanced antigen delivery and targeting to crucial immune cells.